   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "title": "City block (read me first)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "A whole city district, all primitive operations + groups, not a single hand-placed point.\n\n① Lots: a 9×9 grid of 12 m cells; Poly Extrude only insets without extruding (distance 0) to leave room for streets, Blast keeps the inset faces = 81 lots; a Wrangle computes heights on the primitives (taller towards the centre, rand by @primnum, in prim context @P is the face centre), crown heights and numbers; another inset ring separates the sidewalks.\n\n② Buildings: extrude by the prim attribute height (Local Control's Distance Attribute); Group Create's base says @height > 28 to select the tall buildings, Group Combine intersects them with the top faces, first inset to make a setback terrace, then extrude the tower by crown.\n\n③ Facades: Divide's Bricker cuts the walls into 1.6 m × 3.2 m window cells (floor lines align automatically), the ground floor is selected with a bounding box and made into recessed shopfronts, every other cell is inset + pushed in = window frame and glass; roofs are inset and sunk to make parapets.\n\n④ Details: AC units scattered on the roofs, street trees scattered on the sidewalks (pushed apart with Point Relax), each building picks a colour scheme by its number, 12% of windows are lit. All colours are written on prims (Color's Class is also set to prim): when merging, every part's Cd is on the same class, so you don't get half point colours and half primitive colours."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
